From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Frida Hou <Frida-a@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 23:28:36 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] [Spec decode] Reduced draft vocabulary for drafters sharing
 the target lm_head (B17)

speculative_config.draft_vocab_ids = path to a JSON/.npy list of sorted,
unique target ids. The MTP drafter projects onto those Vd rows through a
separate lm_head built from the same checkpoint rows (NVFP4 rows + block
scales + global scales, processed by the head's own quant method), so a
subset logit equals the matching full-head logit; the target keeps its
full head. Greedy drafts take the subset argmax mapped to target ids;
probabilistic drafts scatter the subset logits into a persistent
full-vocab row that is -inf elsewhere, so q is exactly the subset softmax
(q=0 outside) and rejection sampling stays lossless. Load logs Vd, head
bytes and a self-check vs the full head. VLLM_SPEC_DRAFT_VOCAB=0 ignores
the option (old path). TP=1 only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
